WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.033
-Our next guest
can be seen hosting

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.868
"The Second Best Night
of Your Life"

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:08.033
at Union Hall in Brooklyn,
New York, October 30th.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.701
Making their
"Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:12.300
please welcome
the very funny Sabrina Wu!

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.300
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.434
-Thank you.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.167
Hey, everyone.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:28.734
I have some impressions
for you all. Okay.

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:30.467
First impression.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.467
[ Imitates small splash ]

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:35.367
That was a hot girl pooping.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.734
Second impression.

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:45.934
[ Raises, lowers voice ]

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.100
That was the economy.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:53.534
That's all I know about it.
Okay, last impression.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.534
[ Beat-boxing ]

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
Stop, stop. Stop.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.334
That was nothing.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:17.801
I grew up in Michigan,
where they made us read

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:21.267
this widely taught, critically
acclaimed children's book

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:23.901
"Tikki Tikki Tembo."

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:27.701
First page, it goes, "There once
was a Chinese boy named

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:33.968
Tikki Tikki Tembo-no Sa Rembo
Chari Bari Ruchi-pip Peri Pembo.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.934
No, there wasn't.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:43.701
I have a Chinese brother.
His name is Kevin.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:49.501
And, actually,
can we do an experiment?

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.801
Group experiment.
I'm going to say real Chinese.

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:52.968
And then, at some point,

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:55.868
I'm going to switch to
not quite Chinese,

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:57.734
but I won't tell you when.

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:00.601
You tell me when.

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:01.934
Cool.

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:03.934
[ Speaking Chinese ]

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:13.534
Tikki Tikki Tembo-no Sa Rembo
Chari Bari Ruchi-pip Peri Pembo!

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:15.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:20.734
Wow. Wow.

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:22.367
You know, I've told
that joke a million times.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.767
You are the first group
that has gotten it.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:27.667
No, obviously not.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:30.167
So, growing up,
I had this complex,

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.267
this inferiority complex,
where I was like,

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:32.400
"Oh, my God, oh, my God.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.067
I'll do anything
to make a white person like me."

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:36.200
I learned all this --
I learned how to beat-box. Why?

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.400
Why do I know how to do this?

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:43.767
13 years old, I could do this.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:52.033
Honestly, I was training
for Bar Mitzvahs.

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:54.934
One time, I was in a closeted,
label-less relationship

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:57.300
with this white woman,
who, a year in, was like,

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.601
"I love you so much.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:02:59.767
You mean the world to me.

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.334
Do you want to be
my squirrel-friend?"

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:03.968
She said "squirrel-friend"

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:06.033
'cause "girlfriend"
was too scary.

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:08.734
And I, instead of being like,
"We're done," I went...

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:10.734
[ Chuckles, clicking tongue ]

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:17.801
So, yeah, I don't have always
a ton of gay pride, okay?

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:20.801
I realized a year and a half ago
that I was trans,

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.934
and I was like,
"What do you mean some people

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.133
don't have to be gay at all,

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:27.901
and I have to be gay twice?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.534
I have to come out to

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:33.100
my nervous, immigrant
parents again?

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.667
I was like,
"Hey, Dad, I'm trans."

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.868
And my dad went,
"Well, I'm driving!"

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:49.701
And, honestly, I always
suspected he might be a driver.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.167
At some point I was like,
"So, you know,

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:59.067
I'm thinking about going on 'T,'
taking testosterone."

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:02.033
And my dad was like, "Okay,
you don't like your body?

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:04.167
Well, do you think
I like my face?

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.334
Do you think I like my skin,
my eyes?"

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:07.834
He kept going.

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:15.434
I had to pause coming out to be
like, "No, Dad, don't be sad.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:18.167
You're so sexy."

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:24.467
So, yeah, I, like,
really need a win.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.267
I really need one.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:31.334
I'm in the
most humiliating rivalry.

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:35.567
When I was in college, I took a
cute little storytelling class.

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:38.100
And one day,
we went to Moth StorySLAM,

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.534
and I went up and did terrible.

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:43.801
And then this girl from my class
went up, won the whole thing.

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:46.267
And everyone was like,
"Oh, my God.

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.634
She's going to be famous.
She's such a good performer."

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:49.767
And I literally said,

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:50.968
"I'm the one
who's going to be famous.

00:04:50.968 --> 00:04:53.601
I'm the good performer."

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:57.968
It's been six and a half years,
and I'm...

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:02.100
Look, the "Tonight Show"
is a huge honor.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.234
I'm so happy to be here.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:09.067
So, it's just that
that girl is literally

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:14.601
inaugural Youth Poet Laureate
Amanda Gorman.

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:16.167
If you don't remember,

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:19.901
she performed poetry
at Biden's inauguration.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:23.367
People sort of say
she united the country.

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:27.501
Michelle Obama
said she changed her life.

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:29.033
She's been on
the cover of "Vogue."

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:31.300
She's hosted the Met Gala.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.601
She's a "New York Times"
best seller.

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:36.067
If she becomes a staff writer on
"Big Mouth," I will die.

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:42.567
Did you know that she's running
for president in 2036?

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:46.467
I'm going to have to
vote for her.

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.200
And I thought,
you know, in college,

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.834
maybe she was
a little overconfident,

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:52.200
because she would
literally say like,

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.534
"You know, one day,
I might be, like,

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:54.834
the first
black woman president."

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.801
When I was in college,
my big dream -- I was like,

00:05:57.801 --> 00:06:02.567
"Maybe one day I could be, like,
an Asian Jack Black."

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:04.901
I'm Sabrina Wu.
Thank you so much!

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:08.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.834
-One day. Maybe one day.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:12.534
That was so good.

00:06:12.534 --> 00:06:15.567
Sabrina Wu!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:17.801
See Sabrina October 30th

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:20.734
at Union Hall
in Brooklyn, New York.

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.300
We'll be right back, everybody.

